Offer forwarding only where the instance receives forwarded mail.

The API already reports forwarding.enabled in /v1/mailboxes/connect-options
(INBOUND_SECRET or INBOUND_SMTP_ADDR set), but the mailbox wizard always offered
"Forward mail to opendesk" first and marked it Recommended. On an instance with
no inbound route that address never receives anything. When forwarding is off
and IMAP is on, the wizard leaves it out, recommends the first sign-in that needs
no server settings (Email password on a detected host), and the mailbox page
hides "switch to forwarding". With IMAP off, forwarding stays the only way in.

